# DoodleDuel AI — Deployment Guide (Google Cloud / Firebase)

The app ships with **real AI predictions** (DoodleNet — the actual Quick, Draw!
neural network, 345 classes) and **Firebase Realtime Database** for multi-device
multiplayer (admin on a laptop, players on phones).

---

## 1. One-time Firebase setup (keys)

1. Go to <https://console.firebase.google.com> → **Add project**
2. In the project, click the **</> (Web)** icon → register an app named `doodleduel`
3. Firebase shows a `firebaseConfig` object — these are your keys
4. In the left menu: **Realtime Database** → **Create Database** → start in
   **locked mode** → copy the database URL
   (looks like `https://YOUR-PROJECT-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com`)
5. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in every value:

   ```bash
   cp .env.example .env
   ```

6. Restart the dev server. The console warning
   `[DoodleDuel] Firebase env vars missing` should be gone.

> **Are the keys secret?** No. Firebase web API keys identify the project —
> access control is done by **Realtime Database rules** and **Authorized
> Domains** (Hosting → settings), not by hiding the key.

## 2. Local verification

```bash
npm run dev
```

- Tab A → **Host Game** → note the room code
- Tab B (or a phone on the same network with `npm run dev -- --host`) →
  join with username + code
- The admin lobby should list the player instantly; drawing, submissions,
  timer, and AI reveal all sync live.

## 3. Deploy to Google Cloud (Firebase Hosting)

```bash
npm install -g firebase-tools
firebase login
firebase use --add            # pick the project you created
npm run build
firebase deploy               # hosting + database rules in one shot
```

Your game is live at `https://YOUR-PROJECT.web.app`.

### After first deploy

- Firebase Console → **Realtime Database → Rules** → verify the published
  rules match `database.rules.json` (the deploy above pushes them)
- Hosting → **Add custom domain** if desired

## 4. What runs where

| Concern | Where it runs | Needs keys? |
|---|---|---|
| Multiplayer rooms, players, submissions, game phase | Firebase Realtime Database | Yes (`.env`) |
| DoodleNet AI predictions | Browser via ml5.js CDN | No |
| Static hosting | Firebase Hosting (Google Cloud CDN) | No |

## 5. Cost / limits

Realtime Database free tier (Spark): 1 GB storage, 100 simultaneous
connections — plenty for classrooms/parties. DoodleNet (~5 MB) is fetched
once per browser and cached by the CDN.